## 2. Routing Ownership Matrix

| Path | Owner | Priority | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| `/` | app | 10 | catch-all |
| `/api/health` | app | — | container healthcheck |
| `/login` | app | — | redirect-only handler; link with `<a>` |
| `/logout` | app | — | redirect-only handler |
| `/admin` | backend | 100 | native admin |
| `/checkout` | backend | 100 | native checkout |
| `/graphql` | backend | 100 | API |
| `/api/webhooks/*` | app | 110 | must bypass bot protection |
| `/_next/*` | app | 10 | build assets |

Rules:
- Exactly one owner per path; priorities must make ties impossible.
- Bot/WAF protection is per router; callback routers omit it.
- Never proxy callback paths to the backend when the app owns the redirect.

